@page "/privacy"
<PageTitle>Privacy Policy | VitalReach Wellness Hub</PageTitle>
<LegalDocument Title="Privacy Policy" Path="/privacy" Sections="Sections" Description="How we handle information from website visits, messages, shopping, consultation intake and authorized administration. Health information receives separate clinical access controls.">
<section id="who-we-are" tabindex="-1">
<h2>1. Who we are and how to contact us</h2>
<p>VitalReach Wellness Hub is a Ghanaian-American wellness brand offering wellness products, education and consultation intake. “We,” “us” and “our” refer to VitalReach Wellness Hub.</p>
<address><b>VitalReach Wellness Hub</b><br />24 Kusia Street, Kokomlemle, Accra, Ghana<br /><a href="tel:+14105044449">+1 (410) 504-4449</a><br /><a href="/contact">Contact the VitalReach team</a></address>
<p>For a privacy request, provide a way to reach you and, if relevant, your submission or order reference. Do not include symptoms, medical histories, passwords, card details or identity documents in the general contact form. We will explain how to provide any information needed to verify and handle your request.</p>
</section>
<section id="information-collected" tabindex="-1">
<h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Messages:</b> name, email, phone, message content, submission time and read status.</li>
<li><b>Shopping and orders:</b> browser shopping-session identifier, bag contents, product variants and quantities, contact and delivery details, order notes, quotes, shipping and taxes, payment currency and references, payment status and fulfillment history.</li>
<li><b>Consultation intake:</b> name, age, sex response, pregnancy/postpartum response, optional contact information, selected checklists, health answers, dated readings and lab results, medicines and remedies, and notes you provide.</li>
<li><b>Clinical records we create:</b> screening flags and supporting answers, submission reference, consent time and version, review status, and clinical assessment and action notes.</li>
<li><b>Administration and security:</b> sign-in identity, account status and permissions, reviewer identities, access/review audit events and technical logs.</li>
</ul>
<p>Health questions may concern kidney, cardiovascular, liver or diabetes history, medicine use and withdrawal, mental wellbeing, and self-harm. Uncertain answers can remain “Unknown” or “Prefer not to say.” Do not guess measurements.</p>
</section>
<section id="consultation-consent" tabindex="-1">
<h2>3. Consultation consent and choices</h2>
<p>When online intake is available, we ask for affirmative consent before storing your submission for consultation and automated screening review. Opening a QR link, browsing, purchasing a product or accepting general website terms does not give consent to collect a health questionnaire.</p>
<p>The QR code opens a blank form and contains no patient record or health answers. A submission reference is not a public link to your record. You may decline online submission and ask staff about assessment options. Omitting optional information or declining answers may limit the review.</p>
<p>Ask staff to correct a submitted answer or discuss withdrawing consent for future consent-based use. Withdrawal does not undo prior lawful use or necessarily require deletion of records that must be retained.</p>
</section>
<section id="screening-analysis" tabindex="-1">
<h2>4. Automated screening and human review</h2>
<p>Our software applies predefined rules to reported symptoms, history, medicines and measurements to highlight concerns. It records the rule version and reasons for each flag. The current feature does not send questionnaire answers to a generative-AI provider to produce flags.</p>
<p>Flags are not diagnoses or disease probabilities. Incomplete or inaccurate answers can produce missing or incorrect flags. A lack of flags does not mean a person is healthy. A clinical reviewer interprets the information; green “no outstanding action” status records an explicit reviewer decision.</p>
<p>You can ask for an explanation, correction or human review. The tool does not automatically decide eligibility for insurance, employment, credit or treatment. It does not dispatch emergency services or guarantee an immediate response.</p>
</section>
<section id="purposes" tabindex="-1">
<h2>5. Why we use information</h2>
<p>We use information to respond to requests, maintain shopping bags, prepare and fulfill orders, calculate taxes, verify payments, prepare consultations, support clinical review, administer access, investigate problems, prevent abuse and meet applicable recordkeeping obligations.</p>
<p>Consent supports the optional health-intake collection described above. Other processing may be needed to take requested steps toward a purchase, perform an order, protect the service or comply with law. The basis and rights that apply depend on the information, purpose and jurisdiction.</p>
<p>We do not sell personal information. Consultation answers, screening flags and clinical notes are not used for advertising, marketing audiences or newsletter enrollment. Submitting a message, order or consultation form does not sign you up for marketing.</p>
</section>
<section id="access-and-sharing" tabindex="-1">
<h2>6. Access and sharing</h2>
<p>Authorized operational administrators handle messages and orders. Consultation records in the portal require separate clinical-review permission. Superadmins manage permissions; ordinary administrator or superadmin status alone does not grant clinical-record access. Record reads and review updates are audited.</p>
<p>Hosting, infrastructure and support providers may process stored information or backups as needed to operate and secure the service. Payment providers receive payment setup details; tax providers receive delivery and transaction details; fulfillment partners may receive information needed for an arranged delivery. Health questionnaire answers are not supplied to payment or delivery providers as part of these workflows.</p>
<p>Information may also be disclosed as required or permitted by law, to address a safety/security concern, or as part of a lawful business transfer with appropriate protections. Separate clinical referrals or additional health-record disclosures should be discussed with you and handled on an appropriate legal basis.</p>
</section>
<section id="payments" tabindex="-1">
<h2>7. Payments and order records</h2>
<p>When enabled, payments take place on hosted Stripe or Paystack pages. We send setup details such as email, order/reference identifier, amount and currency, and receive verification/status information. Our checkout form does not collect full card numbers or bank login credentials.</p>
<p>Order details, payment references, tax evidence and fulfillment records support service, reconciliation and recordkeeping. Providers handle their own records under their policies: <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe privacy</a> and <a href="https://paystack.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Paystack privacy</a>.</p>
</section>
<section id="sign-in" tabindex="-1">
<h2>8. Google sign-in and administrator records</h2>
<p>Google authenticates approved administrators. We use basic identity information such as email, name, account identifier and sign-in status to control access and attribute activity. We do not request Gmail, Drive, calendar, contact-list or Google password access.</p>
<p>We maintain account status, permissions and relevant administrative records. We do not sell Google sign-in data or use it for advertising. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a> for its handling of information.</p>
</section>
<section id="cookies-and-sessions" tabindex="-1">
<h2>9. Cookies, forms and connections</h2>
<p>Essential cookies support the shopping bag, access to this browser's orders, administrator authentication and request security. The shopping cookie lasts up to 30 days. Clearing it or changing browsers can remove browser access to prior orders without deleting the stored order. Keep your order reference for support. Admin sessions expire and may renew during active use.</p>
<p>Unsubmitted form entries are processed in a temporary server session while you use interactive pages. A short disconnection may permit recovery, but expiry, restart, closing or reloading can lose unsaved entries. Health drafts are not saved in browser local storage. Consultation records are stored when you submit successfully.</p>
<p>The current website does not use advertising pixels or behavioral-advertising cookies. External fonts and an embedded Google map may send technical information such as IP address and browser details to their providers. Following social or other external links is subject to those services' policies.</p>
</section>
<section id="technical-records" tabindex="-1">
<h2>10. Technical records and safeguards</h2>
<p>Servers may record IP addresses, request paths, times, browser information and errors. Connection diagnostics record events without questionnaire answers. Submission limits use a temporary derived network-address identifier to reduce abuse.</p>
<p>Safeguards include HTTPS, encryption of stored consultation answers and clinical notes, separate clinical permissions, restricted server access and audit records. Basic metadata, such as reference, time, urgency and status, is stored separately. Authorized technical personnel may require controlled infrastructure access. No system can promise absolute security.</p>
<p>Use a private device where possible, sign out of shared admin sessions and close a shared visitor session when finished. If a security incident requires notice, we will provide notice as required by applicable law.</p>
</section>
<section id="retention" tabindex="-1">
<h2>11. Retention and backups</h2>
<p>Retention depends on the record and purpose: messages for resolving enquiries; orders/payments for fulfillment, accounting and disputes; consultation records for review, follow-up and applicable clinical recordkeeping; and security/audit records for investigating access and misuse.</p>
<p>Records do not automatically disappear when a consultation is reviewed, a browser closes, consent is withdrawn or an administrator is removed. The current intake service has no automatic deletion deadline. Contact us for applicable retention information or to request deletion; we will consider the purpose and any legal need to retain the record.</p>
<p>Backup copies may remain after a live record is removed until the relevant backup is retired. If deletion is restricted or delayed, we will explain the reason and available options, subject to applicable law.</p>
</section>
<section id="your-rights" tabindex="-1">
<h2>12. Your requests and rights</h2>
<p>Depending on applicable law, you may request access, a copy, correction, deletion, restriction or objection to certain uses, withdrawal of consent, or an explanation and human review of automated processing. We may need proportionate information to verify identity and locate your record. Legal exceptions may apply.</p>
<p>Start through our <a href="/contact?message=I%20would%20like%20to%20make%20a%20privacy%20request.%20Please%20contact%20me%20about%20the%20next%20steps.">privacy request form</a> or center staff. Do not include your health history in that initial message. You can also raise concerns with the competent authority, including Ghana's <a href="https://dpc.gov.gh/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data Protection Commission</a> where applicable.</p>
</section>
<section id="children-and-international" tabindex="-1">
<h2>13. Age limits and international processing</h2>
<p>Online consultation intake is for adults aged 18 and above. Visitors under 18 should ask staff about assisted assessment; the site has no parental-consent workflow for online intake. The general website is not directed to children under 13. Contact us if a child has submitted information inappropriately.</p>
<p>VitalReach serves Ghana and the United States. Processing may occur where our operations and providers are located, and protections differ between jurisdictions. Cross-border processing remains subject to applicable requirements; using this website does not waive statutory privacy rights.</p>
</section>
<section id="policy-updates" tabindex="-1">
<h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>Revisions will carry a new date/version. We will provide further notice or request consent where required for a material change. Updating this policy does not by itself authorize a new use of previously collected health information. Questions can be sent using the contact details in section 1.</p>
</section>
</LegalDocument>
